<title>FRANCE: ADP postal traffic up 7.5pct in 1996.</title>
<headline>ADP postal traffic up 7.5pct in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Paris airports, Charles de Gaulle (CDG) and Orly, handled 128,864 tonnes of postal traffic in 1996, up 7.5 percent on the previous year, Paris airport authority (ADP) figures show.</p>
<p>The number of flights wholly dedicated to postal traffic totalled 7,840 an increase of 19.0 percent on 1995. - Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax:5017</p>
</text>
